From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PP: run the DFlash2 draft tail on an earlier stage

VLLM_PP_DRAFT_TAIL_STAGE (default -1 = off; the compose uses 2). Port of
Morrowmake's switch (v1/worker/gpu/pp_draft_tail.py): the drafter's tail
(candidate lm_head pass, top-k, candidate selector, selector walk) runs on
the given pipeline stage instead of the last one; that stage keeps a copy of
lm_head and the selector and roots the draft-token broadcast. Unsupported
configurations fail at start-up. Includes the audit hardening: the tail's
persistent GEMM and FlashInfer top-k buffers are prepared inside the model
memory profiler (before KV sizing); FlashInfer top-k scratch is isolated
from the main stream only after a start-up probe of the deployed package
(unknown cache contracts fail closed); mHC rejects non-power-of-two hidden
sizes; ContextVar scopes are reset. Validation aid:
VLLM_PP_DRAFT_TAIL_VERIFY (default 0) re-runs the tail on the last stage and
counts rows whose received drafts differ.

